 "findings": {
  "common_to_all": "0 of 64 executed episodes pass the frozen contact policy.",
  "not_one_cause": "the failure is NOT a single cause: the two tasks fail in different classes.",
  "T7_cream_cheese": "every forbidden contact in the representative case is class finger_link_on_target (the finger-link collision geom adjacent to the pad, on the grasp target itself, during grasp/lift). forbidden_by_class.other = 0, so clean_if_finger_link_on_target_allowed = True. This is a POLICY-DEFINITION question: the frozen policy allows only the pad to touch the target.",
  "T0_tomato_sauce": "the representative case has 2 contacts of class 'other': body gripper0_right_gripper touching tomato_sauce_1_main at 12.8 N over 64 control steps (grasp/lift/transport/place) and alphabet_soup_1_main at 8.7 N over 67 control steps (grasp/lift/transport). The static geom dump shows gripper0_right_gripper carries exactly one collision geom, gripper0_hand_collision (the palm mesh), and no finger geom, so this is NOT a classification error: it is a real non-finger body pressing on the objects for most of the carry. It affects BOTH the requested object and the non-requested object held at the fixed plan, so it is not caused by the force request.",
  "consistency_check": "across all 64 stored episodes, every T0 episode has >=1 forbidden contact at >=5 N and every T7 episode has none, which is consistent with the two causes above but does not by itself prove the class composition of the other 62 episodes."
 },
